en on magazines television and her  image  over 70 years has  made itself known to  millions billions of people across the  globe  and  i think because she's a benign presence  she is not a challenging presence she  doesn't have to be a politician  who is trying to prove something she is  just who she is and that's how  she managed to keep that act going for  so long  and she has i suppose in some ways  maintain what you know which is a  strange system not many countries in  europe all around the world have have a  system with a constitutional monarchy  what do you think the future of the  monarchy is without queen elizabeth well  the the curious thing about her was it  didn't it looks like she didn't actually  change but she changed a great deal and  for example if you look at her clothes  um they became more modern as time went  on she  [Music]  got the aura of the age if you like her  and she knew  um  very much to inch forward very slowly  without appearing to do so i think that  whoever well who we know who is coming  next uh may find it hard to  have such a a subtle play  we know that it's king charles iii is  going to be the title don't we  i mean how will he follow  what you know all these leaders and you  and many commentators have been saying  an incredible incredible act from the  from the queen well it's going to be  very difficult for him and of course  what he's going to have to do is take  his foot off the pedal he's got to  learn not to interfere with politics uh  the spider  the spider handwriting memos which he  sent to  cabinet ministers have to cease if he is  to maintain that authority as an  independent figure  which is above and beyond politics  that's what the great success of the  queen's reign was that she never once  interfered politically and uh i think  prince charles uh  with his heart very much in the right  place uh has tried to interfere and i  think it's just going to learn not to do  it and in terms of the royal family  itself clearly they've not had the  easiest of times recently and this is a  personal  point of mourning for them but how do  you think they'll react as a family do  you think they'll come together after  this or do you think that the fractures  will continue to be there  i think that's possibly the first  challenge which king charles will face  uh he has got to either knock heads  together or talk to people and try to  bring um a sense of unity back to this  fractured  uh royal family and  we cannot deny the fact that in the last  couple of years as the queen has ailed  uh that we have seen the wheels slightly  falling off the royal train  christopher wilson thank you very much  indeed coming to talk to us thank you  reminder now the top story

